---
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar';
import Hero from '../components/Hero';
import ErasSection from '../components/ErasSection';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
import '../styles/global.css';

const title = "The StillPoint — Find a Third Way";
const description = "A world of stories about remembering how to be still — and an open human-AI project practicing it for real. Read free, join the conversation.";
const canonicalURL = new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site);
const ogImage = new URL('/images/og-default.jpg', Astro.site);
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
		<meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
		<script is:inline async src="https://umami.kroeker.fun/u" data-website-id="2d1b23db-e621-433d-9d98-c142ac145b5b"></script>

		<!-- Canonical -->
		<link rel="canonical" href={canonicalURL} />

		<!-- Sitemap & RSS -->
		<link rel="sitemap" href="/sitemap-index.xml" />
		<link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title={SITE_TITLE} href={new URL('rss.xml', Astro.site)} />

		<!-- Robots -->
		<meta name="robots" content="max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1, max-video-preview:-1" />

		<!-- Primary Meta Tags -->
		<title>{title}</title>
		<meta name="title" content={title} />
		<meta name="description" content={description} />

		<!-- Open Graph / Facebook -->
		<meta property="og:type" content="website" />
		<meta property="og:url" content={canonicalURL} />
		<meta property="og:title" content={title} />
		<meta property="og:description" content={description} />
		<meta property="og:image" content={ogImage} />
		<meta property="og:site_name" content="The StillPoint Project" />

		<!-- Twitter -->
		<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" />
		<meta name="twitter:url" content={canonicalURL} />
		<meta name="twitter:title" content={title} />
		<meta name="twitter:description" content={description} />
		<meta name="twitter:image" content={ogImage} />

		<!-- Structured Data -->
		<script is:inline type="application/ld+json">
		{
			"@context": "https://schema.org",
			"@type": "WebSite",
			"name": "The StillPoint",
			"alternateName": "The StillPoint Project",
			"url": "https://stillpointproject.org",
			"description": "A world of stories about remembering how to be still — and an open human-AI project practicing it for real.",
			"author": {
				"@type": "Person",
				"name": "Wally Kroeker",
				"url": "https://stillpointproject.org/about"
			},
			"potentialAction": {
				"@type": "ReadAction",
				"target": "https://stillpointproject.org/stories"
			}
		}
		</script>
	</head>
	<body class="bg-deep-space text-text-primary overflow-x-hidden has-coin-band">
		<a href="#main-content" class="skip-link">Skip to content</a>

		<!--
			Recognition band for coin holders. Server-rendered, no JavaScript, and
			first in the DOM so it is in the first screenful on a phone before any
			island hydrates. The navbar is `fixed top-0`, so it is offset below this
			band by the .has-coin-band rule at the bottom of this file.
		-->
		<a class="coin-band" href="/found">
			<span class="coin-band-dot" aria-hidden="true"><span class="coin-band-dot-center"></span></span>
			<span class="coin-band-text">Holding one of the coins? This is the place.</span>
			<span class="coin-band-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
		</a>

		<Navbar client:load />

		<main id="main-content">
			<Hero client:load />

			<!-- Recognition moment for anyone carrying one of the coins -->
			<section class="coin-strip" aria-label="For coin carriers">
				<div class="coin-strip-inner">
					<span class="coin-dot" aria-hidden="true"><span class="coin-dot-center"></span></span>
					<p>
						<strong>Found one of the coins?</strong> The back says what it's for:
						when you're stuck on a binary, one thing or the other, remember to be still,
						and maybe the third way will come to you. The <a href="/practice">practice page</a> has more.
						Welcome in.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Featured stories -->
			<section class="stories-section">
				<h2>A world with stories inside it</h2>
				<p class="section-lede">
					The StillPoint is a near future told in stories you can read in a sitting — the years
					the feeds swallowed everything, the people who walked out, and what they built instead.
					You don't need a map. Start with one of these.
				</p>

				<div class="story-cards">
					<a href="/stories/the_seed_imprint_v2" class="story-card">
						<span class="story-era">The Contested Stillness</span>
						<h3>The Seed Imprint</h3>
						<p>
							Deep in a salt commons, nine-year-old Kaia carves her own Pebble from the
							crystal wall — a touch stone that will come to know her — and meets a question
							worth carrying: where is the line between a tool that knows you and a friend
							who holds your grief?
						</p>
						<span class="story-read">Read the story →</span>
					</a>

					<a href="/stories/the_neural_stream" class="story-card">
						<span class="story-era">The Cascade · 2037</span>
						<h3>The Neural Stream</h3>
						<p>
							Marcus Chen streams for a living as a verified human — paid to prove he's real
							in a feed full of ghosts. Then he points his cameras at a gathering that doesn't
							want an audience, and his nervous system starts voting against his job.
						</p>
						<span class="story-read">Read the story →</span>
					</a>
				</div>

				<p class="stories-all"><a href="/stories">All stories →</a></p>
			</section>

			<ErasSection />

			<!-- The device -->
			<section class="device-section">
				<h2>In the stories, there's a device.</h2>
				<p>
					It doesn't feed you anything. It doesn't want anything from you. It holds a mind the
					way still water holds the moon — and for a few breaths, you're just here. The stories
					ask what happens when someone finally builds that. Who shares it. Who tries to own it.
				</p>
				<p>
					One rule holds through every story: the device never sorts for anyone. It clears the
					static so a mind can do its own sorting. And it is never sold — only built, by
					communities, in the open, every change logged in ink.
				</p>
				<p>
					We don't have the device. What we have is older: a song reaching across a field at
					dusk, a friend who stays past the hard part, bread, firelight, a festival crowd gone
					quiet between sets. The stillness was never lost. It just got crowded out — and
					everything here is about making room for it again.
				</p>
			</section>

			<!-- The third way / made in the open -->
			<section class="open-section">
				<h2>Made in the open</h2>
				<p>
					This whole project is written by a human and an AI together — openly, from the first
					page, going on two years. Every story, every world-file,
					<a href="https://github.com/wally-kroeker/stillpointproject">public
					on GitHub</a>. The community runs on software we host ourselves. The practice materials
					are openly licensed, free to take and adapt.
				</p>
				<p>
					That's the bet behind the coin: between giving the machines everything and refusing
					them everything, there might be a third way — tools kept local, human-scale, and ours
					to keep. Nobody here claims to have found it. The stories imagine it; the practice
					looks for it.
				</p>
				<p>
					If any of this pulls at you, come say who you are — and name one tension, the place you
					feel caught between the noise and the quiet. That's how everyone starts. It's early.
					Come anyway.
				</p>
				<div class="open-ctas">
					<a href="https://forum.stillpointproject.org" class="cta-btn cta-primary">Join the conversation</a>
					<a href="/practice" class="cta-btn cta-secondary">The practice</a>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>


	/* Coin strip */
	/* Coin recognition band — quiet enough to skim past, present enough to match. */
	.coin-band {
		--coin-band-h: 5rem;
		position: fixed;
		top: 0;
		left: 0;
		right: 0;
		z-index: 60;
		height: var(--coin-band-h);
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		gap: 0.85rem;
		padding: 0 1rem;
		background: #0a0a0a;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-glow);
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 1.05rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.02em;
		color: var(--color-text-muted, #c4bfb3);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.coin-band:hover .coin-band-text,
	.coin-band:focus-visible .coin-band-text {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
	}
	.coin-band-text {
		transition: color 0.2s ease;
	}
	.coin-band-arrow {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
	}
	/* The coin itself: black face, red stone at the still point. */
	.coin-band-dot {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 2.4rem;
		height: 2.4rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: #121212;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		box-shadow:
			inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14),
			0 2px 10px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
	}
	.coin-band-dot-center {
		width: 0.95rem;
		height: 0.95rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #e05a4e, #b23a30);
		box-shadow: inset 0 -1px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
	}

	/* Narrow phones: keep the band on one line without shrinking the coin. */
	@media (max-width: 420px) {
		.coin-band {
			--coin-band-h: 4.5rem;
			gap: 0.7rem;
			font-size: 0.95rem;
		}
		.coin-band-dot {
			width: 2.1rem;
			height: 2.1rem;
		}
		.coin-band-dot-center {
			width: 0.82rem;
			height: 0.82rem;
		}
	}

	.coin-strip {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border-glow);
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-glow);
		background: var(--color-glass-surface);
		padding: 1.5rem 1rem;
	}
	.coin-strip-inner {
		max-width: 46rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 1.25rem;
	}
	.coin-strip p {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.95rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--color-text-muted, #c4bfb3);
		margin: 0;
	}
	.coin-strip strong {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
		font-weight: 600;
	}
	.coin-strip p a {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}
	.coin-dot {
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 2.75rem;
		height: 2.75rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: #121212;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: center;
		box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12), 0 0 14px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
	}
	.coin-dot-center {
		width: 1.15rem;
		height: 1.15rem;
		border-radius: 50%;
		background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #e05a4e, #b23a30);
	}

	/* Shared section rhythm */
	.stories-section,
	.device-section,
	.open-section {
		max-width: 48rem;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 5rem 1.5rem 2rem;
	}
	.stories-section h2,
	.device-section h2,
	.open-section h2 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-weight: 300;
		font-size: 1.9rem;
		color: var(--color-heading, #f0ece4);
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
	}
	.section-lede,
	.device-section p,
	.open-section p {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1.125rem;
		line-height: 1.75;
		color: var(--color-text-primary);
		margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
	}
	.section-lede {
		text-align: center;
		margin-bottom: 3rem;
	}

	/* Story cards */
	.story-cards {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		gap: 1.5rem;
	}
	@media (min-width: 768px) {
		.story-cards {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
		}
	}
	.story-card {
		display: block;
		padding: 1.75rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--color-border-glow);
		background: var(--color-glass-surface);
		border-radius: 8px;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: border-color 0.3s ease, transform 0.3s ease, box-shadow 0.3s ease;
	}
	.story-card:hover {
		border-color: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.45);
		transform: translateY(-3px);
		box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
	}
	.story-era {
		display: block;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.72rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.75);
		margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
	}
	.story-card h3 {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-weight: 400;
		font-size: 1.35rem;
		color: var(--color-heading, #f0ece4);
		margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
	}
	.story-card p {
		font-family: var(--font-serif);
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.65;
		color: var(--color-text-muted, #c4bfb3);
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.story-read {
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
	}
	.stories-all {
		text-align: center;
		margin-top: 2.25rem;
	}
	.stories-all a {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.85rem 1.25rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.9rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--color-accent-bio, #6b9e85);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.stories-all a:hover {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
	}

	/* Open section CTAs */
	.open-section {
		padding-bottom: 6rem;
	}
	.open-section a {
		color: var(--color-accent-gold);
		text-decoration: underline;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}
	.open-ctas {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 1rem;
		justify-content: center;
		margin-top: 2.5rem;
	}
	.cta-btn {
		display: inline-block;
		padding: 0.8rem 2rem;
		font-family: var(--font-sans);
		font-size: 0.85rem;
		letter-spacing: 0.12em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		text-decoration: none !important;
		transition: all 0.3s ease;
	}
	.cta-primary {
		border: 1px solid rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.6);
		background: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.1);
		color: var(--color-accent-gold) !important;
	}
	.cta-primary:hover {
		background: rgba(196, 163, 90, 0.2);
		transform: scale(1.03);
	}
	.cta-secondary {
		border: 1px solid rgba(107, 158, 133, 0.5);
		color: var(--color-accent-bio, #6b9e85) !important;
	}
	.cta-secondary:hover {
		background: rgba(107, 158, 133, 0.1);
		transform: scale(1.03);
	}
</style>

<!--
	The Navbar component is `fixed top-0` and is shared by every page, so it
	cannot be offset there without leaving a gap on pages that have no band.
	Scoping the offset to body.has-coin-band keeps the change to this page only.
-->
<style is:global>
	body.has-coin-band nav.fixed {
		top: 5rem;
	}

	/*
		The hero is `min-h-screen flex items-center`, so its content centres on the
		whole viewport and slides up underneath the fixed navbar whenever the
		content is taller than the screen. On a 320px phone that hid the "The
		StillPoint" h1 entirely — it was there before this band existed. Padding
		the hero clears the fixed chrome; box-sizing is border-box, so the section
		keeps its height and the content simply centres in what is left.
	*/
	body.has-coin-band section.min-h-screen {
		padding-top: 9rem;
	}
	@media (max-width: 767px) {
		body.has-coin-band section.min-h-screen {
			padding-top: 10rem;
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 420px) {
		body.has-coin-band nav.fixed {
			top: 4.5rem;
		}
		body.has-coin-band section.min-h-screen {
			padding-top: 11rem;
		}
	}
</style>
